      "body": "Repair head: `ab9630d089386b6d712f88cc828757667359c4ef`.\n\nThe selected existing artist is now retained through the supported email claim form. The Google API does not accept a claim target, so the dialog explains the email path and hides Google signup while a claim is selected; late Google callbacks are rejected before authentication or navigation. Ordinary Google signup remains covered and available. This avoids silently creating a different profile or inventing a new account-linking contract.\n\nCurrent main `6f77a7eec93d96de36840a13235adff9ad13c917` is incorporated by a normal merge. The catalog conflict was resolved by a three-way comparison of individual decision IDs, preserving independent decisions from both parents. The backend test configuration retains main's threaded runtime and two capabilities, including the artist concurrency requirement.\n\nExecuted on the repaired tree: LoginPage and ArtistOnboardingPage 11/11 tests; UI TypeScript and focused ESLint passed; UI production build and initial bundle budget passed (357,170 gzip bytes); release tests 64/64; CI-pipeline tests 23/23; strict catalog audit and whitespace checks passed. No local full backend, database migration, or native-device success is claimed for this follow-up. Exact-head hosted CI and renewed independent approval are required before merge. No manual deployment was performed.\n",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
